module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.expression_enclosing_a_block_headed_operand_lowers_to_that_block_at_v2_body_lowering

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data expression_enclosing_a_block_headed_operand_lowers_to_that_block_at_v2_body_lowering: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "expression_enclosing_a_block_headed_operand_lowers_to_that_block_at_v2_body_lowering" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an expression that CONTAINS a block-headed sub-expression (a match or an if) lowers to that block alone, and normalize ACCEPTS the module** (INVALID STATE: the lowered value of `t && match w {..}`, `t && u && match w {..}`, `t || match w {..}`, `t && if c {..} else {..}`, `R { v: match w {..}, d: q }` and `h(a: match w {..}, b: c)` is the match or if by itself. The enclosing operator, record or call is gone, along with every sibling operand, field, argument, tag and callee, and there is no diagnostic.) The value the program computes is the block's value, whatever the rest of the expression said. When the types agree, as with Bool operands, that wrong answer type-checks. A name in any dropped sibling never reaches resolve, so an undeclared one is accepted.",
    "WHERE, cited by symbol. `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_body_subtree_lower_control_forms` asks `body_lower_find_control_form_optional` for the if/match/loop/let nearest the root, in one pre-order walk. It then lowers THAT form as the whole value. The walk's own comment states the assumption, 'the form nearest the root ... on an expression spine is the one that owns the body', and it is false whenever the control form is an operand, a field value or an argument of an enclosing expression the fold did not lower. The route into it is the fall-back: `body_lower_value_lowered` falls through to `body_lower_body_subtree_lower` when the bottom-up fold leaves the value unlowered, which is the case for these enclosing forms. Then `body_lower_body_subtree_lower_rest` reaches the control-form search.",
    "RECEIPTS. Fixtures, traced by a scratch normalized-tree dump over `v2.compiler.program_assembly` `program_assembly_phase_normalize` at main 8bf4b66774c, and by the census line of each: all six forms above lower to the block alone. The block as LEFT operand (`match w {..} && t`) and the parenthesised form (`t && (match w {..})`) are REFUSED at normalize, not dropped. Census: `v2.compiler.reference_conservation_census` `reference_conservation_census_for_paths` over `reference_conservation_stratified_sample_paths` at 69e0bb7566e. Around 113 atoms absent in accepted modules sit in a && or || chain beside a block, plus the largest residue declarations: `v2.std.float` `float_body_compare_ieee_ordered_outcome` (`Accepted { value: match a {..}, diagnostics: None }`) and `test.claim.codex_package_delivery_wet_witness_test`, whose witnesses are `&& match ..` chains, so a claim there can hold on its last conjunct alone.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. Not `lowering_accessor_collapses_a_sequence_operand`, which keeps the LEFT element of an operand; here the block is kept and the enclosing expression is lost. Not gunbc#11911, a parse-order defect; here the parse accepts. Not `match_arms_after_the_second_are_dropped_at_v2_body_lowering`, which loses arms INSIDE a match; this loses what is AROUND it.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor (silent wrongness). CEILING: structurally guaranteed. An expression lowers to its own operator, construct or application over every constituent, or refuses at the constituent it could not read. A control form is lowered as the whole value only where it IS the value. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: v2 body lowering has no reader that answers a value by searching its subtree for a control form, so an enclosing expression the fold left unlowered refuses instead of being replaced. Owner: bright-boar-848's fold queue (quiet-seal-543, 2026-09-25). The fall-back reader is that lane's subject. Pinned drops, each holding while the drop happens and redding when the repair lands, in `v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.reference_conservation_accepted_drops`: `a_binary_operand_beside_a_match_is_reported_dropped_holds`, `a_binary_operand_beside_an_if_is_reported_dropped_holds`, `a_record_field_beside_a_match_valued_field_is_reported_dropped_holds`, `a_call_argument_beside_a_match_valued_argument_is_reported_dropped_holds`. The census's clean control, `v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.reference_conservation` `the_clean_control_conserves_every_authored_atom_holds`, is the neighbour that conserves.",
    "CLIMBED, THE TRIGGER CAPABILITY MET (bright-boar-848, XL-2). Two links, both in `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold`. (1) `body_lower_find_control_form_optional` no longer searches a value's subtree: it descends only through what does not change the expression -- a production to its captured child, a sequence whose right side is an empty tail, a lone opening or closing delimiter -- so a control form is lowered as the whole value only where it IS the value, and an enclosing operator, call or record goes whole to the binary/postfix route. (2) That route then exposed the second link: `body_lower_primary_expr` ran its raw-syntax strategy readers over a capture the bottom-up fold had ALREADY lowered (a Match or Branch) and one answered it with its first child, so `t && match w {..}` became `t && w`. Measured by calling `body_lower_value_read` at each production level of the operand: correct at the match_expr node, collapsed from its primary parent up. A primary whose capture is core substrate is now that node, the rule `body_lower_postfix_lowered_primary_optional` already states one level up. The four pinned drops flip to conservation controls (accepted AND the enclosing constituent not dropped), red against the base fold and green after. The label and let-binder atoms that stay absent in the same fixtures are the separately declared NamedArgumentLabel and StatementLetBinder drops. RUNG NOW: structurally guaranteed for the enclosing expression.",
    "THE LEFT-OPERAND HALF IS STILL OPEN, and it is valid dag the corpus writes: a block-headed expression as the LEFT operand of a binary operator (`match w {..} && t`, `match w {..} || t`) at expression start. Measured occurrence count 179 (a scan of dag/ and src/v2 for a statement-initial `match .. {` whose closing brace is followed by a `&&`/`||` line); all sit under dag/test, which the native route does not admit into its population, so the native census shows none of them. The seed parser accepts the form and v2 refuses it, so the two parsers disagree on the same source. LOCATED SPECIMEN (gunbc#12758): v2.test.claim.body_lowering.map_literal `ml_the_key_law_names_both_occurrences_holds` is `match map_introduction_duplicate_key(..) { .. } && match .. { .. }`; claim_batch (seed) runs it PASS, and the v2 native route file-refuses src/v2/test/claim/body_lowering/map_literal_test.dag with parse_g0_tokens_remain (WholeFile). Bisected by feeding each top-level declaration to the v2 parser alone: only that declaration refuses. The specimen keeps its spelling as the witness; it is not rewritten around the gap. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the v2 grammar admits a block-headed primary as the left operand of a binary operator, and this specimen's file clears parse on the native route.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.reference_conservation_accepted_drops", decl_name: "a_binary_operand_beside_a_match_is_conserved_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.reference_conservation_accepted_drops", decl_name: "a_binary_operand_beside_an_if_is_conserved_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.reference_conservation_accepted_drops", decl_name: "a_record_field_beside_a_match_valued_field_is_conserved_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.reference_conservation_accepted_drops", decl_name: "a_call_argument_beside_a_match_valued_argument_is_conserved_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
